.TH ZERODDS-WEBDDS-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-webdds-bridged \- OMG Web-Enabled DDS 1.0 gateway daemon (REST + SOAP)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-webdds-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-listen\fR \fIADDR\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-type\fR \fINAME\fR=\fIFILE\fR]...
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-webdds-bridged
exposes DDS applications, participants, topics, publishers,
subscribers, data writers and data readers as HTTP resources, per OMG
Web-Enabled DDS 1.0. Serves the REST PSM under
.IR /dds/rest1 ,
the SIMPLE-WSDL-SOAP PSM under
.IR /soap ,
and the WSDL description of both the fixed object-model operations and
any config-named IDL
.I interface
under
.IR /wsdl ,
all on the one HTTP port.
.PP
A topic's wire type is resolved from a config-named
.I .idl
file
(\fItypes:\fR) or from a peer's TypeLookup discovery — never from an
opaque byte guess. Sample bodies (write/read) are the DDS-WEB XML
representation, converted through the type's own descriptor.
.PP
Every REST request needs an
.B Accept
header naming
.I application/dds-web+xml
(exactly \(em DDS-WEB 1.0 defines no other representation): missing is
400, one naming none of it is 406, and a
.B Content-Type
naming anything else is 415.
.PP
A
.BR create_participant / create_publisher / create_subscriber
body, and its
.B update_*
counterpart, may carry nested
.IR publishers / subscribers / data_writers / data_readers
(OMG DDS-WEB 1.0 \(sc7.4.3.1/\(sc7.4.3.2/\(sc7.4.4.7/\(sc7.4.4.8/
\(sc7.4.4.11/\(sc7.4.4.12): the daemon reconciles the live DCPS
entities against them by name on every call. A
.I qos
or
.I qos_profile
element inside any of them, and any top-level
.B update_*
body, resolves the same way: an inline
.I <qos>
merges onto the entity's current QoS, and a
.I <qos_profile>name</qos_profile>
reference resolves through the daemon's own QosLibrary/QosProfile
metadata first, with an inline
.I <qos>
present alongside it overriding the named profile's values. On
.BR update_* ,
an
.I absent
container element (no
.IR <publishers> ,
say) leaves that kind of contained entity untouched; an
.I empty
one deletes every one of them.
.PP
Implements
.IR "OMG Web-Enabled DDS 1.0, formal/2014-12-01" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
Path to the config file (YAML). See
.BR zerodds-webdds-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-listen =\fIADDR\fR
HTTP bind address. Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1:8080 .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-type =\fINAME\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Type source override (repeatable):
.I NAME
is the IDL scoped name
(\fIMod::Type\fR), also the DDS wire type name;
.I FILE
is the
.I .idl
file it is declared in.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
TLS server cert, PEM; enables
.IR https:// .
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
TLS server key, PEM.
.TP
.BR \-\-auth\-token =\fISECRET\fR
Bearer token auth.
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listener (\fI/metrics\fR).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version info.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM stops the daemon: new connections stop being accepted, an open
connection finishes its current request/response and closes.
.PP
SIGHUP reads the configuration again: the per-Application ACL and the
auth settings apply from then on, TLS cert/key material is re-read from
its configured path. Changed listen address or domain need a restart
and are logged. A configuration that does not load changes nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 2
Bind error \(em address in use.
.TP
.B 3
DDS discovery error.
.TP
.B 4
TLS setup error.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/webdds-bridged.yaml .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-webdds-bridged.yaml (5).
